REM  pench.pni — PENCH, the Physical Embodiment Cycler
REM  PANINI program: a programmable lifecycle for taking a human conception
REM  through physical-system specification, engineering, realization,
REM  integration, packaging, commissioning, acceptance, operation and iteration.
REM
REM  PENCH is the lifecycle.
REM  Holy Grail Labs is the realization substrate.
REM  The cycler is NOT a sequence of prompts; prompts are operations inside stages.
REM
REM  Canonical family:
REM    MATBA  print
REM    KHWAB  visual
REM    AWAZ   audio
REM    TILASM  immersive
REM    PENCH  physical embodiment
REM    YADEIN  personal/life record
REM
REM  Resolution EASY / MID / PRO is orthogonal to lifecycle structure.
REM  AI providers are replaceable execution resources.
REM  Simulation is not experiment; proposed/derived results do not become
REM  physical evidence without the appropriate evidence gate.

CYCLER PENCH
  TITLE   "PENCH"
  SCRIPT  "پنچ"
  OUTPUT  PHYSICAL
  UNIT    "physical artefact"
  PURPOSE "Take a human conception through conceptualization, requirements, architecture, design, simulation, realization strategy, BOM and build/buy decisions, procurement/fabrication, assembly, integration, verification, packaging, commissioning, acceptance, operation and maintenance."

  CONTRACT
    INVARIANT "The cycler builds and preserves thought before physical realization."
    INVARIANT "Requirements, architecture, design and implementation are distinct artefacts."
    INVARIANT "Every approved artefact is versioned and its provenance is preserved."
    INVARIANT "Changing an approved upstream artefact may invalidate dependent downstream artefacts."
    INVARIANT "BOM is a decision stage, not merely an output file."
    INVARIANT "Every realizable component has an auditable realization strategy."
    INVARIANT "Simulation evidence is distinct from physical measurement."
    INVARIANT "A physical artefact is not operational merely because it has been assembled."
    INVARIANT "Packaging and commissioning are lifecycle states."
    INVARIANT "Human approval is required at configured lifecycle gates."
    INVARIANT "Holy Grail Labs supplies realization capability; PENCH specifies and governs the lifecycle."
    REFUSE    "treating a prompt response as proof of physical realization"
    REFUSE    "claiming a component was fabricated, procured, tested or commissioned without evidence"
    REFUSE    "promoting simulation results to physical experimental evidence"
    REFUSE    "silently changing an approved requirement"
  END CONTRACT

  RESOURCE HOLY_GRAIL_LABS
    TYPE REALIZATION_SUBSTRATE
    PURPOSE "Provide heterogeneous physical and computational realization capabilities."
    CAPABILITIES
      FABRICATE
      MACHINE
      PRINT
      ASSEMBLE
      COMPUTE
      ELECTRONICS
      MECHANICS
      SOFTWARE
      INTEGRATION
    END CAPABILITIES
  END RESOURCE

  STATE MACHINE PENCH_LIFECYCLE
    STATE CONCEIVED
    STATE CAPTURED
    STATE SPECIFIED
    STATE REQUIREMENTS_APPROVED
    STATE ARCHITECTED
    STATE ARCHITECTURE_APPROVED
    STATE DESIGNED
    STATE DESIGN_APPROVED
    STATE SIMULATED
    STATE REALIZATION_PLANNED
    STATE PROCURED
    STATE FABRICATED
    STATE ASSEMBLED
    STATE INTEGRATED
    STATE VERIFIED
    STATE PACKAGED
    STATE COMMISSIONED
    STATE ACCEPTED
    STATE OPERATIONAL
    STATE MAINTAINED
    STATE RETIRED
  END STATE MACHINE

  STAGE CONCEPTUALIZE
    RESOLUTION EASY
    VERB   ELICIT
    EXPECT CONCEPT
    INTO   concept
    ASK
      Describe what you want the physical artefact to accomplish.
      Do not design it yet. Capture the intended outcome, users or actors,
      environment, capabilities and important constraints.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(concept)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
    SET STATE CONCEPTUALIZE -> CAPTURED
  END STAGE

  STAGE CAPTURE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   STRUCTURE
    EXPECT SPECIFICATION
    FROM   concept
    INTO   captured_concept
    ASK
      Convert the concept into a structured physical-system concept.
      Capture:
      purpose, users, use cases, operating environment, desired capabilities,
      mobility, sensing, actuation, communication, autonomy, human interaction,
      safety, dimensions, energy, maintainability, cost, availability,
      lifetime and deployment context.
      Preserve unresolved items explicitly.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(captured_concept)
    VALIDATE NO_UNTAGGED_UNKNOWN(captured_concept)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE USE_CASES
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   ELICIT
    EXPECT LIST
    FROM   captured_concept
    INTO   use_cases
    ASK
      Derive the principal use cases for the proposed physical artefact.
      For each use case identify actor, goal, environment, trigger,
      expected behaviour and success condition.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COUNT(use_cases) > 0
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE REQUIREMENTS
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   FORMALIZE
    EXPECT REQUIREMENTS
    FROM   captured_concept, use_cases
    INTO   requirements
    ASK
      Transform the captured concept and use cases into testable engineering
      requirements. Every requirement must have an identifier, subject,
      normative statement, priority, acceptance/test criterion and status.
      Distinguish required, desired, constraint and unresolved requirements.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE UNIQUE_IDS(requirements)
    VALIDATE TESTABLE(requirements)
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(requirements, captured_concept)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE REQUIREMENTS_REVIEW
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVIEW
    EXPECT REVIEW_RECORD
    FROM   requirements
    INTO   requirements.review
    ASK
      Attack the requirements for ambiguity, contradiction, omission,
      non-testability, hidden assumptions and unbounded scope.
      Produce defects and proposed corrections.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(requirements.review)
  END STAGE

  STAGE REQUIREMENTS_REVISION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVISE
    FROM   requirements, requirements.review
    INTO   requirements
    ASK
      Apply only justified corrections. Preserve prior revision history,
      provenance and unresolved items.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE VERSIONED(requirements)
  END STAGE

  STAGE REQUIREMENTS_SIGNOFF
    VERB   GATE
    GATE   HUMAN "SIGNOFF requirements"
    REQUIRE requirements.review.status == COMPLETE
    EMIT   requirements.baseline
    SET    requirements.status = APPROVED
    SET STATE REQUIREMENTS_APPROVED
  END STAGE

  STAGE EMBODIMENT_ARCHITECTURE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   DERIVE
    FROM   requirements
    INTO   architecture
    ASK
      Derive a physical-system architecture from the approved requirements.
      Identify system boundaries and subsystems covering, as applicable:
      mechanical structure, electronics, computation, sensors, actuators,
      communications, power, thermal systems, structural elements, software,
      firmware, control, human-machine interface, environmental interfaces,
      safety systems, enclosure, tooling and manufacturing architecture.
      Record interfaces and dependencies explicitly.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(architecture, requirements)
    VALIDATE INTERFACES(architecture)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE ARCHITECTURE_REVIEW
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVIEW
    FROM   architecture
    INTO   architecture.review
    ASK
      Attack the architecture against every approved requirement.
      Identify missing subsystems, incompatible interfaces, unsafe assumptions,
      capacity constraints, single points of failure and unresolved dependencies.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(architecture.review)
  END STAGE

  STAGE ARCHITECTURE_REVISION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVISE
    FROM   architecture, architecture.review
    INTO   architecture
    ASK
      Revise the architecture while preserving traceability and revision ancestry.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(architecture, requirements)
  END STAGE

  STAGE ARCHITECTURE_SIGNOFF
    VERB   GATE
    GATE   HUMAN "SIGNOFF architecture"
    REQUIRE architecture.review.status == COMPLETE
    EMIT   architecture.baseline
    SET    architecture.status = APPROVED
    SET STATE ARCHITECTURE_APPROVED
  END STAGE

  STAGE DETAILED_DESIGN
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   DERIVE
    FROM   architecture, requirements
    INTO   design
    ASK
      Produce the detailed engineering design.
      Specify dimensions, interfaces, component characteristics, tolerances,
      electrical and mechanical details, computational resources, software/
      firmware boundaries, control interfaces, safety mechanisms, manufacturing
      constraints, calibration requirements and verification methods.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(design, architecture)
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(design, requirements)
    ON FAIL REPAIR
  END STAGE

  STAGE DESIGN_REVIEW
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVIEW
    FROM   design
    INTO   design.review
    ASK
      Review the detailed design for requirement coverage, architectural
      consistency, manufacturability, serviceability, safety, interfaces,
      testability and realization feasibility.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(design.review)
  END STAGE

  STAGE DESIGN_REVISION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVISE
    FROM   design, design.review
    INTO   design
    ASK
      Apply justified design corrections and preserve complete revision ancestry.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE VERSIONED(design)
  END STAGE

  STAGE DESIGN_SIGNOFF
    VERB   GATE
    GATE   HUMAN "SIGNOFF design"
    REQUIRE design.review.status == COMPLETE
    EMIT   design.baseline
    SET    design.status = APPROVED
    SET STATE DESIGN_APPROVED
  END STAGE

  STAGE DIGITAL_TWIN
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   CREATE
    EXPECT MODEL
    FROM   design
    INTO   digital_twin
    ASK
      Construct a simulation-ready model or digital twin sufficient to evaluate
      the relevant physical, mechanical, electrical, computational, thermal,
      control and environmental behaviours of the design.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(digital_twin, design)
  END STAGE

  STAGE SIMULATE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    EXPECT SIMULATION
    FROM   digital_twin
    INTO   simulation
    ASK
      Execute simulations relevant to the approved requirements and design.
      Record configuration, assumptions, model version, parameters, outputs,
      limitations, uncertainty and reproducibility information.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE EXISTS(simulation)
    VALIDATE SIMULATION_LABELLED(simulation)
    SET STATE SIMULATED
  END STAGE

  STAGE SIMULATION_ANALYSIS
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   VERIFY
    FROM   simulation, requirements
    INTO   simulation.analysis
    ASK
      Determine which requirements are supported, contradicted or unresolved
      by the simulation. Do not call a simulation a physical experiment.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NO_PHYSICAL_CLAIM_FROM_SIMULATION(simulation.analysis)
  END STAGE

  STAGE REALIZATION_PLAN
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   PLAN
    FROM   design, simulation.analysis
    INTO   realization_plan
    ASK
      Define how each required subsystem and component will be realized.
      Select fabrication, procurement, modification, reuse, outsourcing or
      other valid realization strategies and identify dependencies, lead times,
      costs, tooling, certification and availability constraints.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COVERAGE(realization_plan, design)
    SET STATE REALIZATION_PLANNED
  END STAGE

  STAGE BOM
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   GENERATE
    EXPECT BOM
    FROM   design, realization_plan
    INTO   bom
    ASK
      Generate a complete bill of materials.
      For every part capture identifier, description, quantity, requirement
      trace, design trace, source options, estimated cost, lead time,
      compatibility, reliability, maintainability, certification and status.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE UNIQUE_IDS(bom)
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(bom, design)
  END STAGE

  STAGE BUILD_BUY_ANALYSIS
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   DECIDE
    FROM   bom, requirements, realization_plan
    INTO   bom.decisions
    ASK
      For every component compare BUILD, BUY, MODIFY, FABRICATE, PRINT,
      MACHINE, ASSEMBLE, RECOVER, REUSE and OUTSOURCE where applicable.
      Evaluate cost, lead time, capability, reliability, availability,
      maintainability, compatibility and certification.
      Record alternatives, rationale and decision authority.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE DECISION_AUDITABLE(bom.decisions)
  END STAGE

  STAGE BUILD_BUY_GATE
    VERB   GATE
    GATE   HUMAN "SIGNOFF realization strategy"
    REQUIRE bom.decisions.status == COMPLETE
    EMIT   realization.baseline
  END STAGE

  STAGE PROCUREMENT
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   EXECUTE
    FROM   bom.decisions
    INTO   procurement
    ASK
      Execute or prepare procurement actions for components whose realization
      strategy is BUY, MODIFY, RECOVER, REUSE or OUTSOURCE.
      Record supplier/source, order state, expected delivery, received evidence
      and deviations from the approved BOM.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NO_UNVERIFIED_RECEIPT(procurement)
    SET STATE PROCURED
  END STAGE

  STAGE FABRICATION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    FROM   bom.decisions, design
    INTO   fabrication
    ASK
      Execute or prepare fabrication actions for BUILD, FABRICATE, PRINT,
      MACHINE or equivalent strategies. Record process, material, tooling,
      machine, operator/system, revision and inspection evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE NO_UNVERIFIED_FABRICATION(fabrication)
    SET STATE FABRICATED
  END STAGE

  STAGE ASSEMBLY
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    FROM   procurement, fabrication, design
    INTO   assembly
    ASK
      Assemble realized components according to the approved design.
      Record component identities, substitutions, deviations, assembly steps,
      torque/calibration data where relevant and inspection evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(assembly, bom)
    SET STATE ASSEMBLED
  END STAGE

  STAGE SUBSYSTEM_TEST
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   VERIFY
    FROM   assembly, requirements
    INTO   subsystem_tests
    ASK
      Test each relevant subsystem independently before full-system integration.
      Record procedure, inputs, measurements, units, uncertainty where applicable,
      expected result, observed result and evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE MEASUREMENTS_HAVE_UNITS(subsystem_tests)
  END STAGE

  STAGE INTEGRATION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   INTEGRATE
    FROM   assembly, subsystem_tests
    INTO   integrated_system
    ASK
      Integrate mechanical, electrical, computational, software, firmware,
      sensing, actuation, communications and power subsystems as applicable.
      Verify interfaces during integration and record deviations.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(integrated_system, architecture)
    SET STATE INTEGRATED
  END STAGE

  STAGE SYSTEM_TEST
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   VERIFY
    FROM   integrated_system, requirements
    INTO   system_tests
    ASK
      Execute system-level tests against approved acceptance and verification
      criteria. Record measured evidence, units, uncertainty, configuration,
      procedure and result.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE MEASUREMENTS_HAVE_UNITS(system_tests)
  END STAGE

  STAGE VERIFICATION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   VERIFY
    FROM   system_tests, requirements, architecture, design
    INTO   verification
    ASK
      Establish traceable evidence for every applicable requirement.
      Classify each requirement PASS, FAIL, PARTIAL or UNRESOLVED.
      Do not convert inference or simulation into physical evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COMPLETE_TRACEABILITY(verification, requirements)
    SET STATE VERIFIED
  END STAGE

  STAGE PACKAGING
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   PACKAGE
    FROM   integrated_system, verification, bom
    INTO   release_package
    ASK
      Construct the complete release package.
      Include physical packaging, enclosure/transport configuration,
      mounting, cables/connectors, deployment kit, spares and tools;
      software/firmware, configuration, calibration and manifests;
      manuals, schematics, BOM, maintenance information, provenance,
      test results, certificates and acceptance records.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COMPLETE_RELEASE_PACKAGE(release_package)
    SET STATE PACKAGED
  END STAGE

  STAGE DEPLOY
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   EXECUTE
    FROM   release_package
    INTO   deployment
    ASK
      Deploy the packaged physical artefact to its intended operational environment.
      Record installation state, environmental conditions and configuration.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE CONFIGURE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   CONFIGURE
    FROM   deployment, release_package
    INTO   commissioning.configuration
    ASK
      Configure hardware, software, firmware, networking, operating parameters
      and deployment-specific settings according to the approved release.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE CALIBRATE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   VERIFY
    FROM   commissioning.configuration
    INTO   commissioning.calibration
    ASK
      Perform required sensor, actuator, instrument and system calibration.
      Record procedures, standards, values, tolerances and evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE CALIBRATION_EVIDENCE(commissioning.calibration)
  END STAGE

  STAGE COMMISSION
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   EXECUTE
    FROM   deployment, commissioning.configuration, commissioning.calibration
    INTO   commissioning
    ASK
      Commission the artefact. Verify installation, networking, safety,
      functional operation, calibration, operator procedures and environmental
      readiness. Record all commissioning evidence.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COMPLETE(commissioning)
    SET STATE COMMISSIONED
  END STAGE

  STAGE ACCEPTANCE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   GATE
    FROM   verification, commissioning
    INTO   acceptance
    ASK
      Conduct final acceptance against the approved requirements and agreed
      operational criteria. Identify any deviations, waivers or open items.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE COMPLETE(acceptance)
    GATE HUMAN "ACCEPT PENCH ARTEFACT"
    SET STATE ACCEPTED
  END STAGE

  STAGE OPERATE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   OPERATE
    FROM   acceptance
    INTO   operation
    ASK
      Establish operational use, monitoring, logging, maintenance scheduling,
      incident handling and performance observation.
    END ASK
    SET STATE OPERATIONAL
  END STAGE

  STAGE OBSERVE
    RESOLUTION MID
    VERB   OBSERVE
    FROM   operation
    INTO   observations
    ASK
      Record operational observations, measurements, failures, maintenance
      events, environmental changes and opportunities for improvement.
    END ASK
  END STAGE

  STAGE MAINTAIN
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   MAINTAIN
    FROM   observations
    INTO   maintenance
    ASK
      Determine required maintenance, repair, replacement, recalibration,
      software/firmware update or engineering change. Preserve complete
      provenance and dependency relationships.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE TRACEABLE(maintenance, release_package)
    SET STATE MAINTAINED
  END STAGE

  STAGE ITERATE
    RESOLUTION PRO
    VERB   REVISE
    FROM   observations, maintenance
    INTO   next_revision
    ASK
      Determine whether observed evidence requires revision of requirements,
      architecture, design, BOM, realization strategy, implementation,
      packaging or commissioning. Generate the next controlled revision
      without destroying predecessor states.
    END ASK
    VALIDATE VERSIONED(next_revision)
  END STAGE

  STAGE RETIRE
    VERB   RETIRE
    FROM   operation, maintenance
    INTO   retirement
    ASK
      Retire the physical artefact while preserving provenance, configuration,
      evidence, maintenance history, operational history and final status.
    END ASK
    SET STATE RETIRED
  END STAGE

  LOGIC
    WHEN requirements.changed
      INVALIDATE architecture, design, digital_twin, bom, realization_plan
      INVALIDATE verification, release_package, commissioning
      EMIT "downstream artefacts require impact analysis"
    END

    WHEN architecture.changed
      INVALIDATE design, digital_twin, bom, realization_plan
      INVALIDATE verification, release_package, commissioning
    END

    WHEN design.changed
      INVALIDATE digital_twin, bom, realization_plan
      INVALIDATE verification, release_package, commissioning
    END

    WHEN bom.changed
      INVALIDATE realization_plan, procurement, fabrication, assembly
      INVALIDATE integration, verification, release_package
    END

    WHEN verification.status == FAIL
      ROUTE TO DESIGN_REVIEW
    END

    WHEN simulation.analysis.status == FAIL
      ROUTE TO DESIGN_REVISION
    END

    WHEN acceptance.status != ACCEPTED
      ROUTE TO ITERATE
    END

    AFTER requirements.ITERATIONS >= 3
      GENERATE requirements.summary
      REQUEST HUMAN "REVIEW REQUIREMENTS CONVERGENCE"
    END

    UNTIL requirements.status == APPROVED
      REVIEW requirements
      REVISE requirements
    END

    UNTIL architecture.status == APPROVED
      REVIEW architecture
      REVISE architecture
    END

    UNTIL design.status == APPROVED
      REVIEW design
      REVISE design
    END

    UNTIL verification.status == PASS
      ANALYZE verification.failures
      REVISE affected_artifacts
      RETEST affected_requirements
    END
  END LOGIC

  ARTIFACTS
    ARTEFACT concept
    ARTEFACT captured_concept
    ARTEFACT use_cases
    ARTEFACT requirements
    ARTEFACT requirements.baseline
    ARTEFACT architecture
    ARTEFACT architecture.baseline
    ARTEFACT design
    ARTEFACT design.baseline
    ARTEFACT digital_twin
    ARTEFACT simulation
    ARTEFACT realization_plan
    ARTEFACT bom
    ARTEFACT bom.decisions
    ARTEFACT procurement
    ARTEFACT fabrication
    ARTEFACT assembly
    ARTEFACT integrated_system
    ARTEFACT subsystem_tests
    ARTEFACT system_tests
    ARTEFACT verification
    ARTEFACT release_package
    ARTEFACT deployment
    ARTEFACT commissioning
    ARTEFACT acceptance
    ARTEFACT operation
    ARTEFACT observations
    ARTEFACT maintenance
    ARTEFACT retirement
  END ARTIFACTS

  PROVENANCE
    TRACK concept
    TRACK requirements
    TRACK architecture
    TRACK design
    TRACK bom
    TRACK realization
    TRACK tests
    TRACK verification
    TRACK packaging
    TRACK commissioning
    TRACK acceptance
    TRACK operation
    TRACK maintenance
    HASH all_release_artifacts
    PRESERVE revision_ancestry
    PRESERVE dependency_graph
    PRESERVE evidence_chain
  END PROVENANCE

  RESOLUTION
    EASY
      PURPOSE "Conceptualize and capture a physical artefact at low resolution."
    END
    MID
      PURPOSE "Structure requirements, interfaces, workflows and realization planning."
    END
    PRO
      PURPOSE "Formal engineering specification, verification, provenance and controlled realization."
    END
  END RESOLUTION

  PROVIDERS
    ALLOW REMOTE_AI
    ALLOW LOCAL_AI
    ALLOW USER_API
    ALLOW HUMAN
    ALLOW SYMBOLIC_ENGINE
    ALLOW SIMULATOR
    ALLOW HOLY_GRAIL_LABS
  END PROVIDERS

  EVIDENCE
    CLASS RETRIEVED
    CLASS INFERRED
    CLASS PROPOSED
    CLASS UNRESOLVED
    CLASS SIMULATED
    CLASS MEASURED
    CLASS VERIFIED
    RULE "simulation != measured"
    RULE "proposed != verified"
    RULE "unresolved remains unresolved until evidence resolves it"
  END EVIDENCE

  RELEASE
    REQUIRE requirements.status == APPROVED
    REQUIRE architecture.status == APPROVED
    REQUIRE design.status == APPROVED
    REQUIRE verification.status == PASS
    REQUIRE commissioning.status == COMPLETE
    REQUIRE acceptance.status == ACCEPTED
    PACKAGE concept
    PACKAGE requirements
    PACKAGE architecture
    PACKAGE design
    PACKAGE bom
    PACKAGE realization_plan
    PACKAGE verification
    PACKAGE commissioning
    PACKAGE acceptance
    PACKAGE provenance
    HASH release_package
    EMIT "PENCH physical artefact release"
  END RELEASE

END CYCLER
